entry.summary:
Introduction
I would like to share in this post an important change we've implemented in Equillar: migrating from SecretBox to AEAD (Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data) to protect sensitive data such as the private keys of the system wallets. Originally, Equillar used sodium_crypto_secretbox to encrypt sensitive data. It's a solid and proven algorithm, but after reading Stellar's security guide for web-based projects, we realized we could significantly improve our security by implementing AEAD. Before diving into code, let's understand what we gain with this change: // Only encrypts the message $cipher = sodium_crypto_secretbox($message, $nonce, $key);
Features: ✅ Encryption + authentication of the message ✅ Simple and fast ❌ Doesn't protect associated metadata ❌ Doesn't bind…
